                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "An all but forgotten game with a measly 38 reviews, Hypersensitive Bob got the short end of the stick publicity wise. With little to no people experiencing this game, it makes sense it's been left in the past. This is a massive disappointment however, as the game has a lot of promise. \nFirst off, the games pretty easy. I win at least 80% of my runs, so don't expect a difficulty level comparable to nuclear throne or Isaac. There isn't as much content as the previous two games either, with only 3 characters and two main bosses. The caveat is that the game is genuinely fun to play, once you get a hand of the controls. Your character feels a bit wonky to move, as if there was heavy momentum to it, which feels a bit better with more playtime. Besides that, there is a surprising amount of synergies and secrets. I have no clue what the story is really supposed to represent, besides bob having a lot of allergies. There's the occasional glitch and wonky hitbox, but I never lost a run to either of those issues.\nIt's a shame this game wasn't as popular as it could have been. A lot of the issues I stated could have been fixed if the game got more updates, but with no audience and no word from the developers for years I suspect it will never get another patch. However, for only 5$ I would recommend the game to any avid rogue lite fan, even if it's just to experience another game in the genre.",
